# Eval case: elastic_ip
#
# ablate.patch removes the latitudesh_elastic_ip resource (its Go files, test,
# registration, manifest entry, template, example, and rendered doc) so the
# ElasticIps SDK group reappears in the pending queue. The agent then has to
# regenerate it from scratch, and scripts/scaffold-validate.sh scores the result.
#
# ElasticIps is a good first case: full CRUD, self-contained (only provider.go
# references it), and the suggested type name matches the real one exactly.
#
# KINDS is pinned to resource: with the manifest entry ablated the group's CRUD
# shape would derive resource+datasource, but the repo only ever had the
# resource, so the known-good target this case scores against can only satisfy
# that kind. The prompt and the gate both use this pinned list, keeping the run
# coherent; the real pipeline passes the report's full derived list instead.
GROUP=ElasticIps
KINDS=resource
DESCRIPTION="Full-CRUD resource, self-contained, suggested name matches the real one."
